const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 15 Walkthrough: Fashion Store";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 15 walkthrough for the Fashion Store: the handwritten bill that totals 363,99, the register keypad, the barcode scan that returns code 30015, and the door keypad that ends the level at +5 coins.";
const faqJsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the door code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 2 Level 15, the Fashion Store?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "30015. You do not find it written on a wall: the register prints a receipt after you pay, and running the Barcode reader over that receipt returns a Code item reading 30015. The five digits go into the keypad beside the shop's double doors."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the total on the handwritten bill?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "363,99, with a comma. The bill in the inventory lists 25,50, 299,00, 32,99 and 6,50 in a column and the boxed total under them reads 363,99. The four figures add up to exactly 363,99, and the receipt the register prints repeats the same line items and the same total, which is the cross-check that the reading is right."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where do I find the handwritten bill?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "On the register counter. At 3:15 in our capture the player taps the counter surface next to the printer and the item pops up as Handwritten bill. It is the only pickup on that counter that matters, and without it the register's keypad has no number to accept."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I get the code out of the receipt?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Open the bag, select Barcode reader with cable, press Use, then tap the receipt. The screen switches to a close-up of the receipt inside white corner brackets with a red scan line running across it, and a moment later a white pop-up prints 30015 over the label Code. The receipt itself carries a barcode under the THANK YOU line, which is what the reader is reading."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why will the register not accept my total?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The bill is written in the comma decimal style, so the amount is 363,99 rather than 363.99. The register screen is a bare numeric keypad with a red CLEAR, a red DEL and a green ENTER; type the five characters in the same style the bill uses, check the amount field before you press ENTER, and use CLEAR rather than DEL if a digit goes in wrong, because DEL walks back one character at a time and it is easy to leave a stray figure in front of the amount."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I have to solve the shoe wall and the tile panel to finish the Fashion Store?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "We could not prove either is optional. Our recording works both of them on the way through, and the finish is triggered at the door rather than at any of the display puzzles, so the register chain is the part that is definitely required. Treat the shoe wall, the tile panel, the chest and the four-wheel dial as the room's side puzzles: they hand over items and keep you moving, but this page will not tell you they are skippable because we never saw a run that skipped them."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does the Fashion Store take?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The results screen reads Time 3:57 with an efficiency bar of nine segments out of ten, and the clip itself runs 4:09 because it opens on a title card. That is a fast run by someone who already knew the bill was on the counter. Players who read the bill as 363.97, or who hunt for a code on the walls, routinely spend far longer in the same room."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What do you get for finishing Chapter 2 Level 15?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Five coins and an efficiency rating of nine out of ten. The results screen shows +5 Coins, a ten-segment efficiency bar with nine filled, and Time 3:57. The Piggy Bank panel underneath is the game's own upsell and nothing on it is needed for the room."}}]};
---
