    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the door code in the Fashion Store in Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2?</summary><p><b>30015</b>. It is not written anywhere in the shop. Pay the handwritten bill at the register, take the receipt the printer produces, then use the <b>Barcode reader with cable</b> on it — the scan returns a Code item reading 30015. The keypad beside the double entrance doors takes those five digits and the level ends.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the total on the handwritten bill?</summary><p><b>363,99</b>, with a comma. The four lines are 25,50, 299,00, 32,99 and 6,50, and the boxed total underneath reads 363,99. The arithmetic checks — those four figures sum to exactly 363,99 — and the receipt the register prints after a correct entry repeats the same items and the same total, which is the cross-check that the handwriting has been read right.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Where do I find the handwritten bill?</summary><p>On the register counter at the back of the ground floor. At 3:15 in the recorded run the player taps the counter surface beside the receipt printer and the item pops up as <b>Handwritten bill</b>. It is the only pickup on that counter that matters, and until you have it the register has no amount to accept.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I get the code out of the receipt?</summary><p>Open the bag, select <b>Barcode reader with cable</b>, press <b>Use</b>, then tap the receipt. The view switches to a close-up of the receipt inside white corner brackets with a red scan line running across it, and a moment later a white pop-up prints <b>30015</b> over the label <b>Code</b>. The barcode sits under the THANK YOU line at the bottom of the paper, which is why you cannot simply read the code off the receipt.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why will the register not accept my total?</summary><p>The bill is written in the comma decimal style, so the amount is <b>363,99</b> and not 363.99. The register screen is a bare numeric keypad with a red <b>CLEAR</b>, a red <b>DEL</b> and a green <b>ENTER</b>, plus an amount field along the top. Type the figure the way the paper writes it, check the field before you commit, and use CLEAR rather than DEL if a digit goes in wrong — DEL removes one character at a time and it is easy to leave a stray figure at the front of the amount.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Do I have to solve the shoe wall and the tile panel to finish?</summary><p>We could not prove either is optional. Our recording solves both on the way through, and the finish is triggered at the door rather than at any display puzzle, so the register chain is certainly the required part. Treat the shoe wall, the sixteen-tile panel, the chest and the four-wheel dial as the room's side puzzles: they hand over items and keep the shop busy, but this page will not call them skippable, because we never saw a run that skipped them.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does the Fashion Store take?</summary><p>The results screen reads <b>Time 3:57</b> with an efficiency bar of nine segments out of ten, and the clip runs 4:09 because it opens on a title card. That is a fast run by a player who already knew the bill was sitting on the counter. Nothing in the room is timed and there is no fail state, so a slower first pass costs you nothing but the walk back to the door.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What do you get for finishing Chapter 2 Level 15?</summary><p><b>+5 coins</b> and an efficiency rating of nine out of ten. The results screen shows the +5 badge, a ten-segment bar with nine filled, and Time 3:57. The Piggy Bank panel underneath is the game's own optional upsell and nothing on it is needed to finish the room — five coins is also a small payout for a two-floor level, so this is not a good room to replay for currency.</p></details>

